TITLE      Gamma-ray production cross sections for the            10097  1    6 
            O16 (n,x gamma) reaction from 6.35- to 16.52-mev      10097  1    7 
            neutron energy                                        10097  1    8 
FACILITY   (LINAC) Pulsed 55 MeV electron linear accelerator.     10097  1    9 
            Pulse width 50 nsec, repitition rate 520 pps.         10097  1   10 
INC-SOURCE (EVAP) Evaporation spectrum from Ta-Be target.         10097  1   11 
SAMPLE     Ring-shaped scattering sample of D2O (25.4 cm i.d.,    10097  1   12 
            50.8 cm o.d., and 5.7 cm thick) enclosed in plexiglas 10097  1   13 
            Container, 0.32 cm thick.                             10097  1   14 
METHOD     (TOF) Time-of-flight                                   10097  1   15 
DETECTOR   (GELI) 30 cc Ge(Li) gamma detector                     10097  1   16 
           (SCIN) Flux monitored by calibrated proton-recoil      10097  1   17 
            scintillator (NE-211), 2 in diameter by 2 in long.    10097  1   18 
           50-m evaluated flight path.  Ring scatterer centered on10097  1   19 
            flight path axis.  Ge(Li) detector positioned at an   10097  1   20 
            angle of approximately 125 deg, but sample dimensions 10097  1   21 
            resulted in subtended angle range from 112 to 142 deg.10097  1   22 
MONITOR    Absolute Ge(Li) efficiency determined with             10097  1   23 
            calibrated (+-3%) radioactive sources.  Relative      10097  1   24 
            efficiency curve shape obtained from known relative   10097  1   25 
            intensities of gammas from thermal capture in Fe and  10097  1   26 
            Cl.                                                   10097  1   27 
CORRECTION Corrected for multiple scattering flux attenuation     10097  1   28 
            and for gamma attenuation in the sample.              10097  1   29 
ERR-ANALYS Following errors estimated:                            10097  1   30 
             Absolute neutron flux               about 10%        10097  1   31 
             Ge(Li) efficiency - below 2.7 MeV   about 5%         10097  1   32 
                               - above 2.7 MeV   about 10%        10097  1   33 
             Flux attenuation and multiple                        10097  1   34 
               Scattering                        <5%              10097  1   35 
             Gamma attenuation in sample         <2%              10097  1   36 
           Overall uncertainty, apart from counting statistics,  110097  1   37 
             about 15%.                                           10097  1   38 
